Challenges Faced

During the Kali Linux setup, I had difficulty locating the network settings on the running system.

I had to research how to access the network configuration window and found the "nm-connection-editor" command.

I opened the terminal and ran:

nm-connection-editor

This opened the Network Connections window, which allowed me to access the network settings and continue with the configuration.

Lessons Learned

- How to open network settings using the terminal.
- How to use the "nm-connection-editor" command.
- The importance of researching and troubleshooting when facing technical difficulties.

This experience helped me understand that sometimes using terminal commands can make it easier to access system settings in Linux.
